@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@teamId = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111

### Health check (no credentials needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Alice belongs to Platform and Research
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Authorization: Basic alice demo-password

### Create a note in Platform; saves its ID for the following requests
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes
Authorization: Basic alice demo-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Release checklist",
  "content": "Verify migrations before deployment."
}

> {%
    client.test("Created", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201); });
    client.global.set("noteId", response.body.id);
%}

### Bob can read his teammate's note
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Basic bob demo-password

### Bob can edit the note (version 1 becomes version 2)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Basic bob demo-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Release checklist",
  "content": "Verify migrations and check service health.",
  "version": 1
}

### An edit based on the old version returns 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Basic alice demo-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My outdated edit",
  "content": "This change will not overwrite Bob's edit.",
  "version": 1
}

### Carol is outside Platform and receives 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Basic carol demo-password

### List notes with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Basic alice demo-password

### A teammate can delete the note (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Basic bob demo-password

### The deleted note now returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Basic alice demo-password
